# Line endings and encoding.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# A dozen source files were saved with a UTF-8 byte-order mark by an editor, then
# read as cp1252 by a tool and written back. The result was visible mojibake in
# rendered JSX -- a middle dot arriving as two Latin-1 characters -- across
# student-facing pages. See load/fix-encoding.js.
#
# The BOM was the upstream cause, so this repo now states its expectations rather
# than leaving them to each contributor's editor settings.

# Normalise line endings on commit and check out LF everywhere. The previous
# setup relied on a per-machine core.autocrlf, which is why 146 files disagreed
# and why every `git add` printed an LF->CRLF warning.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source and documentation: LF, and never a BOM.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf

# Windows is already LF via the rules above; .bat/.cmd keep CRLF because cmd.exe
# cannot parse LF batch files.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised -- doing so corrupts them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary